<div class="abstract-box">
  <b>Abstract</b>
  This paper presents the design and functional verification of a novel 3D-stacked hardware
  security logic lock architecture, named 3D Chip Security Logic Lock. The design implements
  a multi-step physical intercept and audit mechanism using three vertically stacked layers.
  The system comprises four core modules:
  (1) <b>forksheet_core</b> (Engine Layer): ARX-transform-based calculation flow processor,
  forcing data upward to the audit layer via vertical VIA logic leap;
  (2) <b>m2_intercept</b> (M2 Audit Layer): PGU logic array executing Five Axioms Check,
  covering Bio-Hash match, Phys-XOR zero verification, entropy check,
  sampling integrity, and truth gate consistency;
  (3) <b>sovereign_base</b> (Brake Layer): upon receiving audit failure, sequentially executes
  back-gate bias adjustment (nanosecond-level), logic gate deactivation,
  and permanent hard-wired shutdown;
  (4) <b>tsv_channel</b> (Vertical VIA Channel): handshake routing protocol between three layers.
  All modules were verified using Icarus Verilog 12.0 on EDA Playground with EPWave
  waveform confirmation. 35 test cases, 100% pass rate, zero latch inferences,
  zero timing violations.
