<h2>1. Introduction</h2>
<p>
Escalating chip supply chain security threats — hardware Trojans, device counterfeiting,
and reverse engineering — demand security mechanisms operating at the physical layer,
beyond what logic-level defenses can provide. In 3D-stacked IC architectures,
the physical separation between silicon dies enables a fundamentally new security dimension:
inter-layer physical interception. By controlling data flow through Through-Silicon Via (TSV)
channels, deploying non-destructive physical audit at the M2 metal layer,
and implementing nanosecond-level hardware forced shutdown in a dedicated brake die,
a "physical logic lock" can be realized that no software attack can bypass.
</p>
<p>
This paper presents the 3D Chip Security Logic Lock: a complete RTL implementation
of this concept, verified using Icarus Verilog 12.0 with EPWave waveform confirmation.
The design targets high-security applications including military, financial, and industrial control systems.
</p>

<h2>2. System Architecture</h2>
<p>
The 3D Chip Security Logic Lock implements a vertically stacked three-layer structure
(Figure 1), with strict functional separation between layers.
</p>

