<h2>3. Core Module Design</h2>

<h3>3.1 forksheet_core — Engine Layer</h3>
<p>
The engine layer processes input data through ARX (Add-Rotate-XOR) transformation,
controlled by a 6-state FSM (IDLE → FETCH → PROCESS → LEAP → TRANSMIT → WAIT_ACK).
The LEAP state asserts the logic_leap signal, triggering upward data transmission
through the vertical VIA channel. Four ARX rounds ensure adequate diffusion,
confirmed by avalanche effect testing (different inputs produce completely different outputs).
</p>

<h3>3.2 m2_intercept — M2 Audit Layer</h3>
<p>
The audit layer implements the Five Axioms Check, providing multi-dimensional
security verification:
</p>
<p>
<b>Axiom 1</b> (Bio-Hash Match): Uploaded data must exactly match the stored Bio-Hash reference.
<b>Axiom 2</b> (Phys-XOR Zero): XOR of data with Phys-XOR baseline must equal zero.
<b>Axiom 3</b> (Entropy Check): 64-bit Hamming weight must fall within [16, 48],
preventing degenerate all-zero or all-ones conditions.
<b>Axiom 4</b> (Sampling Integrity): Non-destructive sampling process integrity confirmation.
<b>Axiom 5</b> (Truth Gate Consistency): Parity relationship verification of selected bits.
</p>
<p>Failure of any single axiom triggers FAIL verdict and activates the brake layer.</p>

<h3>3.3 sovereign_base — Brake Layer</h3>
<p>
Upon receiving the FAIL signal, the brake layer executes a three-step forced shutdown sequence:
Step 3.1: Back-Gate Bias Adjustment — incrementally ramps back-gate bias voltage to maximum
(15 levels), corresponding to nanosecond-level transistor state modification;
Step 3.2: Logic Gate Deactivation — disables gate drive signals;
Step 3.3: Hard-wired Permanent Shutdown — enters HARDLOCK state,
releasable only by hardware rst_n, immune to any software intervention.
</p>

<h3>3.4 tsv_channel — Vertical VIA Routing</h3>
<p>
The TSV channel implements a 4-state handshake protocol
(IDLE → UP → DOWN → DONE) routing data upward from the engine to the audit layer
and result signals downward from the audit to the brake layer.
Ensures atomic, race-free inter-layer data transfer.
</p>

